{"title":"1994 AHSME Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is inscribed in a circle, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e739144567aa6b89202da31613ef2c8480c9fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B = \\angle C = 4\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"138\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are adjacent vertices of a regular polygon of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> sides inscribed in this circle, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/3/3530581e9cd5267e219e657a4fda77a40180dea1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=$\" width=\"29\" height=\"8\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65fef671e3625f7b69731ed1d6f1df3b84df2f51.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(Circle((0,0), 5)); draw((0,5)--(3,-4)--(-3,-4)--cycle); label(&quot;A&quot;, (0,5), N); label(&quot;B&quot;, (-3,-4), SW); label(&quot;C&quot;, (3,-4), SE); dot((0,5)); dot((3,-4)); dot((-3,-4)); [/asy]\" width=\"232\" height=\"252\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/b/61b4384710b637a8e1211137bc78275850c0e0c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 5 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 7 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 9 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 15 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"366\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1ac662f7ddbbce489953c8b7693848239564aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> as follows: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/101b1e67175ca4d20f32212482eea07926fcc003.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4\\angle A+4\\angle A+\\angle A=180\\implies 9\\angle A=180\\implies \\angle A=20^\\circ.\\]\" width=\"459\" height=\"14\" /> That means that minor arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28cc93fbfb5ed16e87ce30594bc806a6094fe106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"20\" /> has measure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3388936ca5d53b685a625b9baac877382e278a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />. We can fit a maximum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/e/4de51135098c2bbfb9658c2731d894e0ebdee387.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{360}{40}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"38\" /> of these arcs in the circle.\n</p><p>--Solution by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=200685\">TheMaskedMagician</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME\" title=\"1994 AHSME\">1994 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1994 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1994 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1994\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1994 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1994 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1994 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1994 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1994 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"